					Post by: <b>JulieC</b> on <b>September 06, 2007, 03:50:20 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">As an update, this trial has been pushed back, yet again, till October....<br /><br />Did you know there are currently three different panels being convened to look at police accountability in this city?<br /><br />Mayor Nickels&#039; got one (some of the people are okay, some are ridiculous, but this panel will be comparing Seattle police accountability to that in other cities which is dumb because everyone&#039;s accountability systems are not functional because they do not deal with the crux of the issue and do not redelegate power), and I think city council is convening one. The Church Council has convened one (don&#039;t trust these fools, they get paid by the city), and the NAACP is convening one (this is our best bet, as they will be looking at police culture itself as a problem.) <br /><br />Aight One. </div>
